<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $24.0 bln on Jan 24.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $24.0 bln on Jan 24.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.99 billion on January 24, 1997 from $23.89 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Jan 24	 Jan 17	Jan 25</p>
<p>					   1997	  1997	  1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,745	19,646	 16,468</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,246	 4,246	  4,457</p>
<p>    SDRs				     6	     6	     48</p>
<p>    Total			     23,997	23,898	 20,973</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
